
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
DB = DC [00]
DA = DB [01]
DE = DA [02]
F,C,A are collinear [03]
EF ⟂ AC [04]
G,B,A are collinear [05]
EG ⟂ AB [06]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. F,C,A are collinear [03] & AC ⟂ EF [04] ⇒  FC ⟂ EF [07]
002. G,B,A are collinear [05] & EG ⟂ AB [06] ⇒  GE ⟂ GB [08]
003. FC ⟂ EF [07] & GE ⟂ GB [08] ⇒  ∠(FC-GB) = ∠FEG [09]
004. G,B,A are collinear [05] & F,C,A are collinear [03] & ∠(FC-GB) = ∠FEG [09] ⇒  ∠EGB = ∠EFC [10]
005. DB = DC [00] & DA = DB [01] & DE = DA [02] ⇒  C,E,B,A are concyclic [11]
006. C,E,B,A are concyclic [11] ⇒  ∠ACE = ∠ABE [12]
007. C,E,B,A are concyclic [11] ⇒  ∠ECB = ∠EAB [13]
008. G,B,A are collinear [05] & F,C,A are collinear [03] & ∠ABE = ∠ACE [12] ⇒  ∠GBE = ∠FCE [14]
009. ∠EGB = ∠EFC [10] & ∠GBE = ∠FCE [14] ⇒  ∠FEG = ∠CEB [15]
010. F,C,A are collinear [03] & G,B,A are collinear [05] & ∠(FC-GB) = ∠FEG [09] ⇒  ∠AFE = ∠AGE [16]
011. ∠AFE = ∠AGE [16] ⇒  G,E,F,A are concyclic [17]
012. G,E,F,A are concyclic [17] ⇒  ∠GFE = ∠GAE [18]
013. ∠ECB = ∠EAB [13] & ∠GFE = ∠GAE [18] & G,B,A are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠EFG = ∠ECB [19]
014. ∠FEG = ∠CEB [15] & ∠EFG = ∠ECB [19] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ΔEFG is similar to ΔECB
==========================
